<Legal
  title="Content & Moderation Policy"
  description="What gets listed on SharedChats, what never does, and how removal works. Listing is not endorsement; entries are removed on valid request."
  lastUpdated="July 26, 2026"
>
  <p>
    SharedChats is a curated index, not an open platform. Every entry is chosen by a human editor.
    This page explains what makes the cut and what never will.
  </p>

  <h2>What gets listed</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Conversations already shared publicly by their own authors on an AI provider's official share feature.</li>
    <li>Conversations that are interesting: technically impressive, funny, surprising, or educational.</li>
    <li>Conversations that can be read without harming anyone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What never gets listed</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Conversations exposing personal data — names, health, finances, or private circumstances of identifiable people.</li>
    <li>Harassment or content targeting individuals or groups.</li>
    <li>Any sexual content involving minors — reported, never indexed.</li>
    <li>Instructions that meaningfully enable violence, exploitation, or serious harm.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Listing is not endorsement</h2>
  <p>
    An entry on SharedChats means an editor found the conversation worth reading — not that we agree
    with anything said in it, or vouch for its accuracy. Many listed conversations are interesting
    precisely because the AI gets things wrong.
  </p>

  <h2>Removal</h2>
  <p>
    Conversation authors, people mentioned in a conversation, and rights holders can request
    delisting by emailing <a href="mailto:hello@sharedchats.com">hello@sharedchats.com</a>. Valid
    requests are honored promptly. Entries whose source links die are also pruned over time.
  </p>
</Legal>
